<div class="research-card" id="aml">
<img src="assets/img/research/placeholder.svg" class="research-thumb" alt="">
<div class="research-body">
<h4 class="research-title">Acute Myeloid Leukemia</h4>
<p class="research-desc">Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore. By tracking subclonal populations before, during, and after treatment, we study how tumors evolve under therapeutic pressure and which clones drive relapse. Methods from the lab (SciClone, ClonEvol, fishplot) support this work.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="research-card" id="clonal-architecture">
<img src="assets/img/research/placeholder.svg" class="research-thumb" alt="">
<div class="research-body">
<h4 class="research-title">Integrative &amp; functional genomics</h4>
<p class="research-desc">Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation. We combine DNA, RNA, single-cell, and epigenomic data to move from lists of variants to mechanistic understanding &mdash; identifying which alterations matter and how they reshape cellular programs.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="research-card" id="immunotherapy">
<img src="assets/img/research/placeholder.svg" class="research-thumb" alt="">
<div class="research-body">
<h4 class="research-title">Designing cancer immunotherapies</h4>
<p class="research-desc">Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate. We contribute computational tooling for neoantigen identification and personalized vaccine design (pVACtools, pVACview) and study how the genomic and immune landscapes of tumors shape response.</p>
